                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef1457c0-dabe-422b-bf37-d50f08b1d8fa",
                                "sense_id": "016a8c41-8658-3f6a-8a5b-649fcebcea72",
                                "text": "What of the weakling, the ignorant criminal? Not who, excuseless,\nBreaking my law braved death, knowing his deed and its due —\nNay, but the feeble and foolish, the poor transgressor, of purpose"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a0768b2-81a0-41bd-aef4-64967458c9f4",
                                "sense_id": "016a8c41-8658-3f6a-8a5b-649fcebcea72",
                                "text": "To accept these and kindred social sicknesses as fatalities is as excuseless as to accept tuberculosis or hookworm as permanent and unavoidable ills."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "78bb0b9f-256d-40b5-9ab6-4d14ae611095",
                                "sense_id": "016a8c41-8658-3f6a-8a5b-649fcebcea72",
                                "text": "1922, Judson Eber Conant, The Church The Schools and Evolution /The Logic of Evolution is Destructive\nThe Bible makes man's fall deliberate and wilful, and his continued attitude of sinful enmity against God, in spite of all God's offered power to change it into love, one of excuseless lawlessness and rebellion."
                            }
